"entity": {
"name": "Hewlett Packard Enterprise Co.",
"description": "Hewlett Packard Enterprise Co. is a global edge-to-cloud company, which engages in the provision of information technology, technology and enterprise products, solutions, and services. It operates through the following segments: Server, Hybrid Cloud, Intelligent Edge, Financial Services, and Corporate Investments and Other. The Server segment consists of general-purpose servers for multi-workload computing and workload-optimized servers, and integrated systems for high-performance computing and supercomputing, artificial intelligence, data analytics, and transaction processing. The Hybrid Cloud segment is involved in cloud-native and hybrid solutions across storage, private cloud, and infrastructure software-as-a-service. The Intelligent Edge segment offers wired and wireless local area networks, campus, branch, and data center switching, SD-WAN, private and public cellular network software, and network security. The Financial Services segment provides leasing, financing, IT consumption, utility programs, and asset management services. The Corporate Investments and Other segment includes Advisory and Professional Services, Communications and Media Solutions, and Hewlett Packard Labs. The company was founded by William R. Hewlett and David Packard on July 2, 1939 and is headquartered in Spring, TX.",
